{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0159ad3uotAT2owTTAVu5bfq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: ralph-loop\n3\tdescription: \"Use when autonomously implementing a PRD task-by-task. Each loop iteration picks one task, TDDs it, commits, exits. Progress persists in git. Triggers: ralph, AFK mode, autonomous loop.\"\n4\tdisable-model-invocation: true\n5\tmetadata:\n6\t  source: mattpocock/ralph-workshop-repo-001 (technique only — no canonical SKILL.md to SHA-sync)\n7\t  adapted-date: \"2026-04-28\"\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t# Ralph Loop\n11\t\n12\tAutonomous implementation loop. Each iteration gets fresh context, picks one task from the PRD, implements it, runs feedback loops, commits, and exits. Progress lives in git history, not conversation memory.\n13\t\n14\t## Setup\n15\t\n16\tThese commands run automatically when the skill loads — output replaces each line below:\n17\t\n18\t- Available PRDs: !`for d in docs/plans/*/; do [ -f \"$d/prd.md\" ] && basename \"$d\"; done 2>/dev/null || true`\n19\t- Project files: !`ls package.json Makefile Cargo.toml go.mod pyproject.toml setup.py 2>/dev/null || true`\n20\t- Tests directory: !`ls tests/ 2>/dev/null || true`\n21\t\n22\t### 1. Select a PRD\n23\t\n24\tFrom the PRD list:\n25\t\n26\t- If the user passed a name (e.g. `/ralph-loop auth-system`), use `docs/plans/auth-system/prd.md`\n27\t- If there's exactly one PRD, use it\n28\t- If there are multiple, ask the user which one to use\n29\t- If there are none, tell the user to run `/prd-create` first\n30\t\n31\tStore the selected PRD path as `PRD_FILE` for use in the prompt template.\n32\t\n33\t### 2. Detect feedback loops\n34\t\n35\tMap the detected project files to feedback commands:\n36\t\n37\t- `package.json` → `npm run test`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`\n38\t- `Makefile` → `make test`, `make check`\n39\t- `Cargo.toml` → `cargo test`, `cargo check`\n40\t- `go.mod` → `go test ./...`, `go vet ./...`\n41\t- `pyproject.toml` / `setup.py` → `pytest`, `mypy`\n42\t- `tests/` directory in this repo → `bash tests/test-skills.sh`, `bash tests/test-structure.sh`\n43\t\n44\tBuild the feedback loop commands list from what's actually available.\n45\t\n46\t### 3. Create the plans directory\n47\t\n48\t```bash\n49\tmkdir -p docs/plans/<name>\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\t### 4. Generate the prompt\n53\t\n54\tPrefer the prompt generator script because it uses the shared loop engine's\n55\tfeedback detector:\n56\t\n57\t```bash\n58\tbash skills/loop/ralph-loop/scripts/prompt.sh <name>\n59\t```\n60\t\n61\tIf running from an installed skill path, resolve `{{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}` as in\n62\tstep 5 and run `bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/prompt.sh <name>`.\n63\t\n64\tThe script writes `docs/plans/<name>/prompt.md`, sources `lib/feedback.sh`,\n65\tand renders feedback commands from `almanac_loop_feedback_markdown()`.\n66\tUse the template below only as a fallback when the script is unavailable.\n67\t\n68\tWrite `docs/plans/<name>/prompt.md` (e.g. `docs/plans/auth-system/prompt.md`) using the template below, filling in the detected feedback loops and the PRD path:\n69\t\n70\t```markdown\n71\t# INPUTS\n72\t\n73\tPull @{{PRD_FILE}} into your context.\n74\t\n75\tYou've been passed the last 10 RALPH commits (SHA, date, full message). Review these to understand what work has been done.\n76\t\n77\t# TASK QUEUE\n78\t\n79\tBefore decomposing the PRD, check whether an explicit queue exists. Detect in this order:\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VBXnEJr4hBEm1954BzWA3K","session_id":"7f32d037-1d78-4726-b16f-75668d38d257","uuid":"f7eb81a0-4728-40e9-8df7-3b0d4411c8cb","timestamp":"2026-05-26T14:25:59.337Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Find architectural friction in almanac"}
