{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011NKX8ghu1t77upBwgZoZYi","type":"tool_result","content":"200\t\n201\t  Interactive CLI:\n202\t    almanac ralph\n203\t    # or: bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/ralph.sh\n204\t\n205\t  Single iteration (HITL):\n206\t    bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/once.sh <name>\n207\t\n208\t  Autonomous (AFK):\n209\t    bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/afk.sh <name> <iterations>\n210\t\n211\t  Example — run 10 iterations:\n212\t    bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/afk.sh auth-system 10\n213\t```\n214\t\n215\tWhere `{{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}` is the absolute path to this skill's scripts. Resolve in this order:\n216\t\n217\t1. `~/.agents/skills/almanac/ralph-loop/scripts` — set by `almanac install codex`; use this when running in Codex.\n218\t2. `~/.claude/skills/almanac/ralph-loop/scripts` — set by `almanac install claude-code`; use this when running in Claude Code.\n219\t3. `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts` — fallback if the host agent populates `CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR` from the resolved skill directory.\n220\t4. `$ALMANAC_HOME/skills/ralph-loop/scripts` — fallback when invoked outside an installed provider.\n221\t\n222\tPrint the literal provider install path in user-facing instructions (`~/.agents/...` for Codex, `~/.claude/...` for Claude Code) so users can run the scripts directly.\n223\t\n224\t## Modes\n225\t\n226\t### AFK Mode (`afk.sh`)\n227\t\n228\tFully autonomous. Runs N iterations, each in a fresh agent context. Stops when:\n229\t- All tasks complete (`<promise>COMPLETE</promise>`)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VBXnEJr4hBEm1954BzWA3K","session_id":"7f32d037-1d78-4726-b16f-75668d38d257","uuid":"7972d2f5-deca-458c-bd8f-61d5a132f0b1","timestamp":"2026-05-26T14:26:28.634Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Find architectural friction in almanac"}
