{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016r3kVpMYSffLhRivm7x3Hf","type":"tool_result","content":"commit d6f859c131f16ef36636e874175ffa87ea898141\nAuthor: converge <converge@almanac>\nDate:   Tue May 26 16:16:08 2026 +0200\n\n    CONVERGE(the-almanac-codebase-improve-gives-no-major-improvements): round 2\n    \n    Two architectural deepenings out of the 8 candidates round 1 surfaced.\n    All 17 test suites green; net -38 LOC.\n    \n    Finding #6 — slug unification.\n      - Deleted `almanac_converge_slug` and `almanac_harden_slug`; both were\n        shallow wrappers over `almanac_loop_slug`.\n      - All callers use the shared resolver directly.\n      - Latent bug fix surfaced while doing this: harden's wrapper used\n        fallback \"target\", but `harden_latest_run_id` uses `loop_slug` with\n        fallback \"run\". So empty-target registrations wrote\n        `harden-target-*` while lookups searched `harden-run-*`. Unifying to\n        the shared resolver eliminates the divergence.\n    \n    Finding #2 — worker-status record (generic TSV record engine).\n      - Replaced the 16-positional-arg `almanac_loop_write_worker_status`\n        with the named-record pattern `almanac_loop_worker_record_set`.\n      - Both run-status and worker-status now go through one generic engine\n        in lib/run.sh — adding a worker field is a one-line addition to\n        `almanac_loop_worker_record_fields`, not a 16-positional-arg writer\n        rewrite plus every callsite.\n      - Tests migrated: test-harden-cli.sh and test-worker.sh now call the\n        record_set form.\n    \n    CONTEXT.md updates: documents converge as the third loop, the slug","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01VBXnEJr4hBEm1954BzWA3K","session_id":"7f32d037-1d78-4726-b16f-75668d38d257","uuid":"61cb28ff-5b9c-47c8-a11c-a6aea63e9b0d","timestamp":"2026-05-26T14:26:42.257Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Find architectural friction in almanac"}
