{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WHLxfpcDmWxPJsYsD2RPyv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0187nN7a8Nh6C6owEqQesBDE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nrefactor(loops): collapse signal_file/control_file duplication; fix harden default provider\n\nFour codebase-improve sweeps:\n\n* signal_file consolidation. Three loop adapters (ralph/harden/converge)\n  each redeclared the identical `.${name}-${kind}` case-statement for\n  stop|steer. Hoisted the pattern into `almanac_loop_default_signal_file`\n  in lib/loops.sh and resolved via `almanac_loop_signal_file` (adapter\n  override else default). Adapters now declare nothing — adding a standard\n  new loop costs zero signal_file code, and three identical cases can't\n  drift apart.\n\n* control_file consolidation. `almanac_harden_control_file` and\n  `almanac_converge_control_file` were near-identical wrappers that joined\n  a base path with the loop's signal-file basename. Replaced both with\n  a single `almanac_loop_run_control_file <type> <base> <kind>` in\n  lib/run.sh; updated 10 callsites; deleted the wrappers.\n\n* harden default provider. lib/harden-core.sh hardcoded \"claude\" as the\n  fallback default for role config, so harden silently broke when claude\n  wasn't installed. Now uses `almanac_provider_default` like converge —\n  active-env provider if available, else first installed (claude → codex).\n\n* ralph-loop SKILL.md fallback path. The \"fallback when invoked outside an\n  installed provider\" pointed at the pre-categorization path\n  `$ALMANAC_HOME/skills/ralph-loop/scripts` — actual path is now nested at\n  `$ALMANAC_HOME/skills/loop/ralph-loop/scripts`.\n\nTests updated to assert at the resolved control-contract surface\n(`almanac_loop_signal_file`) rather than per-adapter dispatch, and the\ndefault's loop-name-independence is pinned directly.\n\nNOTE: tests not run in this session due to sandbox-permission constraints;\nrecommend `bash tests/test-loops.sh && bash tests/test-run.sh` before push.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit refactor"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":388,"cache_read_input_tokens":136897,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":388},"output_tokens":61,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f32d037-1d78-4726-b16f-75668d38d257","uuid":"0919d949-a53f-40ec-b29b-7f0894339ef5","request_id":"req_011CbRM7UpQ3wWqDsLAJyfu1"}
